# Keep the Docker build context lean. Two stages consume it: the Rust builder
# (crates/ + server/ + desktop/) and the spa stage (web/ + workspace manifests,
# since effort 5 the image builds and serves the PWA). Everything below is
# excluded from the context sent to the builder, which speeds up `docker build`
# and avoids cache-busting on unrelated changes (docs/, local artifacts, …).

# --- Rust build output (the builder produces its own, hermetic copy) ---
target/
**/target/

# --- JS / PWA workspace: sources are needed by the spa stage — exclude only
#     local artifacts (the container installs its own node_modules and
#     regenerates the wasm mirror via web/scripts/mirror-wasm.mjs) ---
**/node_modules/
web/dist/
web/dev-dist/
web/.vite/
web/coverage/
web/public/wasm/
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# --- Spikes: manifests only — pnpm-lock.yaml lists them as importers, so
#     --frozen-lockfile needs them on disk; their sources/deps never enter
#     any image (the spa stage installs with --filter @taletrek/web...) ---
spike/**
!spike/piper/package.json
!spike/web-audio/package.json

# --- Root JS config not needed inside any stage ---
biome.json
wrangler.jsonc

# --- Docs + planning (not needed at compile time) ---
docs/
CHANGELOG.md

# --- VCS + editor + caches ---
.git/
.gitignore
.github/
.idea/
.vscode/
.ruff_cache/
opencode.jsonc
.opencode/

# --- Generated bundle dev artifacts (gitignored; never bake into the image) ---
*.taletrek
*.taletrek-lib
# Keep the committed fixtures OUT of the image too — the runbook uploads them
# over HTTP at runtime; the binary does not embed them.
crates/synth/tests/fixtures/

# --- OS / misc ---
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.log
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
LICENSE
README.md
